  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the structural property of whether a lottery includes a sure outcome. However, in this case, neither lottery has a sure outcome, so the reason would not discriminate between them. The individual, in contrast, bases their reasoning entirely on the relative size of the worst possible losses and emotional aversion to larger losses, explicitly stating that probability differences are negligible. There is no mention or consideration of certainty or sure outcomes in the verbal report. The information considered by the individual (loss magnitude, emotional impact, worst-case comparison) does not overlap with the information relevant to the decision reason (presence of a sure outcome). Furthermore, the individual’s justification is based on outcome severity, not structural certainty. Therefore, there is no evidence that the individual used the decision reason.",
